>> title: House Brown Sauce
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: soy, oyster sauce, chinese, stir-fry, stovetop
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: brown sauce, brown gravy, egg foo young gravy, takeout brown sauce, 褐色醬汁
>> servings: 6
>> time: 20 min

>> step: whisk cold, in a saucepan
Whisk @chicken stock{2%cups}(475 mL), @light soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @oyster sauce{2%Tbs}, @dark soy sauce{1%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} together cold in a #small saucepan{}.

>> step: simmer 10 min, lift the aromatics out
Simmer @&(~1)sauce base{} with @fresh ginger{2%slices}(coin-sized) and @garlic{2%cloves}(smashed) for ~simmer{10%min}, then lift both out and discard them.

>> step: thicken 1 min, to coat a spoon
Thicken @&(~1)sauce{} with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(slaked in 3 Tbs cold water), stirring, for ~simmer{1%min}, until it coats the back of a spoon.

>> step: finish off the heat
Stir @toasted sesame oil{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)brown sauce{} off the heat.
